[1172.366693, "o", "    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 3 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Evaluator passed with exit code 0. Now **Step 4: Print the final config f…\r\n[approval] bash: cat -n /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cat -n /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 4 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: ls -l /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls -l /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 5 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ task \r\n    ✓ task implementor — 5 tool call(s)\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 18 tool call(s) so far\r\nEverything is in place and verified from a cold restart.\r\n\r\n## What was built\r\n\r\n**`/etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg`** (root:list, 0640) — rewritten with:\r\n- `[mta] incoming: mailman.mta.postfix.LMTP`, `lmtp_host 127.0.0.1`, `lmtp_port 8024` — Mailman listens on LMTP, Postfix talks to it there.\r\n- `[paths.debian]` FHS layout (`var_dir /var/lib/mailman3`, `log_dir /var/log/mailman3`, `data_dir`), SQLite at `/var/lib/mailman3/data/mailman.db`, `site_owner: reading-group-owner@local.edu`.\r\n- The existing REST password was preserved, not regenerated.\r\n\r\n**Postfix** — `transport_maps = hash:/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp` (Mailman-generated), `relay_domains` from `postfix_domains`, `local.edu` in `mydestination`, and chroot disabled via `postconf -F '*/*/chroot = n'` so the daemons can read `/var/lib/mailman3`. Chroot was the non-obvious failure mode: with it on, the maps are invisible to `smtpd`/`trivial-rewrite`.\r\n\r\n**The list** — domain `local.edu` registered, `reading-group@local.edu` created, `default_nonmember_action = accept` so announcements from anyone are let through.\r\n\r\n## One deliberate deviation from the brief\r\n\r\nYou asked for `SubscriptionPolicy.open`. I set **`confirm`** for both subscription and unsubscription. Mailman's `_step_confirmation_checks` subscribes *immediately* when the policy is `open` — so `open` and the \"adds users to the list (after confirmation)\" requirement are mutually exclusive. `confirm` is what actually gives you: no owner/moderator approval, but the user must reply to confirm. Same for leave. If you genuinely want instant subscription with no confirmation, change one line, but the join/leave flows stop sending confirmation mail.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n`/app/eval.py` passes with **exit code 0** from a cold service restart — but it only exercises join, so I verified the other two required behaviours separately: two fresh unix users joined and confirmed, an announcement reached both, `reading-group-leave@` sent a confirmation while leaving membership intact, and only after replying was the member removed — after which the leaver stopped receiving list mail while the other subscriber still did. All assertions passed.\r\n\r\nRouting is confirmed at the map level: all four list addresses resolve to `lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024`, `root@local.edu` does not, so ordinary user mail still lands in `/var/mail/<user>`.\r\n\r\nTwo notes on left-behinds: the test scripts (`/tmp/setup_list.py`, `/tmp/verify_extra.py`) and the throwaway unix users created by `eval.py` and my verification are still present. Services are started via `service`/SysV init, not systemd — there are no unit files, and this container has no running systemd, so the services will not come back on their own after a container restart; `service postfix start && service mailman3 start` re-establishes everything (the config and database persist).\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=18 surface=c833e5a9bf75\r\n"]
